steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787252004
      nanos: 859246501
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a production-feeling web demo called \"DealPulse\" for a hackathon Stage-1 submission.\n\nPRODUCT ONE-LINER\nDealPulse is an enterprise deal-risk agent that analyzes sales call transcripts + CRM opportunity context, extracts MEDDPICC gaps, scores risk, proposes next-best actions, executes actions through reusable MCP skills, and performs verifiable specialist handoffs (agent\342\206\222agent\342\206\222human) with a full audit ledger.\n\nTRACK POSITIONING\nTrack 2 \342\200\224 Platform Agent Skills & Knowledge.\nEmphasize: reusable MCP skills, skill registry, orchestration, and handoff packets \342\200\224 not just a chatbot.\n\nTARGET USERS\nAccount Executives and RevOps at B2B SaaS companies.\n\nCORE UI (single page app, modern, dense but clean \342\200\224 NOT a purple AI clich\303\251 theme)\nUse a professional enterprise look: dark slate / charcoal base, electric teal accent, crisp typography (not Inter/Roboto defaults if possible), subtle grid or soft gradient atmosphere.\nLayout:\n1) LEFT: Chat / Agent console (conversation with DealPulse)\n2) CENTER: Opportunity Risk Panel\n   - Risk score (0\342\200\223100) + severity badge\n   - MEDDPICC radar or checklist (Metrics, Economic Buyer, Decision Criteria, Decision Process, Paper Process, Identify Pain, Champion, Competition)\n   - Gap list with severity\n   - Next-best actions (actionable cards)\n3) RIGHT: Platform panels (tabs)\n   - Skills (MCP Fabric registry)\n   - Handoffs (timeline + current handoff packet)\n   - Action Ledger (immutable-looking audit log of every tool call / decision)\n4) TOP BAR: product name \"DealPulse\", subtitle \"MCP Fabric \302\267 Verifiable Handoffs\", demo scenario selector, \"Run Demo\" button\n\nDEMO SCENARIOS (hardcoded fixtures; no real OAuth)\nInclude at least 2 scenarios selectable from dropdown:\nA) \"Expanding enterprise \342\200\224 champion weak\" (medium risk)\nB) \"Late-stage legal block \342\200\224 paper process stalled\" (high risk)\n\nEach scenario includes:\n- Fake CRM opportunity JSON (account, ARR, stage, close date, competitors, stakeholders)\n- A realistic multi-speaker sales call transcript (8\342\200\22315 turns)\n- Expected risk themes already implied in the transcript\n\nAGENT BEHAVIOR\nWhen user clicks \"Run Demo\" or asks \"Analyze this deal\":\n1) Call skill: transcript.analyze\n2) Call skill: crm.get_opportunity\n3) Call skill: meddpicc.extract\n4) Update Risk Panel\n5) Propose 3\342\200\2235 next-best actions\n6) Optionally auto-trigger handoff if risk > 70 OR paper-process/legal gaps exist:\n   - Router \342\206\222 Compliance Specialist agent\n   - Show handoff packet (context summary, decisions so far, open questions, recommended owner)\n7) Offer executable actions as buttons:\n   - crm.update_stage\n   - crm.add_next_steps\n   - email.draft_ae_brief\n   - ticket.create_legal_review (for high paper-process risk)\n8) Every tool call appears in Action Ledger with: timestamp, skill name, inputs summary, outputs summary, status, correlation_id\n\nMCP FABRIC (must be visible and central to the story)\nImplement a Skill Registry with these mock MCP skills (local JS functions, not real network MCP yet):\n- crm.get_opportunity\n- crm.update_stage\n- crm.add_next_steps\n- transcript.analyze\n- meddpicc.extract\n- email.draft_ae_brief\n- ticket.create_legal_review\n- handoff.route_specialist\n- handoff.to_human\n\nEach skill card shows: name, description, input schema (short), output schema (short), \"status: mock MCP\".\n\nHANDOFF OS (capability, not separate product)\nShow a vertical timeline:\n- DealPulse (primary)\n- Compliance Specialist (when routed)\n- Human AE / RevOps (escalation)\nHandoff packet JSON viewer (pretty printed) with fields:\n{\n  from_agent, to_agent, reason, risk_score, meddpicc_gaps, decisions_so_far, open_questions, recommended_actions, evidence_quotes[]\n}\n\nCHAT UX\n- Streaming or stepwise status messages (\"Calling transcript.analyze\342\200\246\", \"Updating risk model\342\200\246\")\n- User can ask follow-ups: \"Why is Economic Buyer weak?\", \"Draft the AE brief\", \"Hand off to compliance\", \"Escalate to human\"\n- Cite 1\342\200\2232 short transcript quotes when explaining gaps\n\nTECH REQUIREMENTS (important for later Cloudflare export)\n- Single deployable frontend app (React or vanilla + modern JS is fine)\n- Keep all fixtures in /fixtures or embedded JSON modules\n- Put mock MCP skills in a clear skills/ or mcp/ module with one function per skill\n- Separate \"agent orchestrator\" logic from UI\n- No secrets required for demo path (optional Gemini API key only if you use live LLM; otherwise rule-based + templated analysis is OK for offline reliability)\n- Prefer deterministic demo mode: \"Run Demo\" should always produce a strong, consistent result for judges even if LLM is unavailable\n- Include a DEMO_MODE flag: if no API key, use fixture-derived analysis templates\n\nDETERMINISTIC ANALYSIS ENGINE (required)\nDo NOT rely only on an LLM. Implement a robust heuristic analyzer that:\n- Scans transcript for keywords/phrases for each MEDDPICC element\n- Computes gap severity\n- Computes risk score\n- Picks next actions from a rules table\nThen optionally enhance wording with LLM if available.\nThis makes the demo reliable for Devpost judges.\n\nSAMPLE OUTPUT QUALITY BAR\nRisk panel must look \"investor/demo ready\":\n- Clear score\n- Specific gaps (\"Champion mentioned but no multi-thread to Economic Buyer\")\n- Evidence quotes\n- Actions with owners and due-style suggestions (\"AE: schedule EB meeting this week\")\n\nREADME SECTION IN UI\nInclude a collapsible \"Architecture\" drawer explaining:\nMCP Fabric (skills) \342\206\222 Orchestrator \342\206\222 DealPulse agent \342\206\222 Handoff router \342\206\222 Action Ledger\nPlus \"Stage 2 roadmap\": Freshworks MCP/Agent Studio, ElevenLabs AE voice brief, real CRM connectors, eval traces.\n\nDELIVERABLES IN CODE\n- App runs locally with npm/vite or equivalent\n- Clear file structure\n- Seed fixtures for both scenarios\n- Comments marking where real MCP/Freshworks would plug in for Stage 2\n\nDo NOT build multiple products. Do NOT add Sarvam/ElevenLabs yet. Do NOT add auth. Focus on one rock-solid happy path.\n\nFirst, scaffold the full app with fixtures + deterministic analyzer + UI panels working end-to-end for scenario B (high risk). Then polish scenario A. Then improve visual polish and microcopy."
    items {
      text: "Build a production-feeling web demo called \"DealPulse\" for a hackathon Stage-1 submission.\n\nPRODUCT ONE-LINER\nDealPulse is an enterprise deal-risk agent that analyzes sales call transcripts + CRM opportunity context, extracts MEDDPICC gaps, scores risk, proposes next-best actions, executes actions through reusable MCP skills, and performs verifiable specialist handoffs (agent\342\206\222agent\342\206\222human) with a full audit ledger.\n\nTRACK POSITIONING\nTrack 2 \342\200\224 Platform Agent Skills & Knowledge.\nEmphasize: reusable MCP skills, skill registry, orchestration, and handoff packets \342\200\224 not just a chatbot.\n\nTARGET USERS\nAccount Executives and RevOps at B2B SaaS companies.\n\nCORE UI (single page app, modern, dense but clean \342\200\224 NOT a purple AI clich\303\251 theme)\nUse a professional enterprise look: dark slate / charcoal base, electric teal accent, crisp typography (not Inter/Roboto defaults if possible), subtle grid or soft gradient atmosphere.\nLayout:\n1) LEFT: Chat / Agent console (conversation with DealPulse)\n2) CENTER: Opportunity Risk Panel\n   - Risk score (0\342\200\223100) + severity badge\n   - MEDDPICC radar or checklist (Metrics, Economic Buyer, Decision Criteria, Decision Process, Paper Process, Identify Pain, Champion, Competition)\n   - Gap list with severity\n   - Next-best actions (actionable cards)\n3) RIGHT: Platform panels (tabs)\n   - Skills (MCP Fabric registry)\n   - Handoffs (timeline + current handoff packet)\n   - Action Ledger (immutable-looking audit log of every tool call / decision)\n4) TOP BAR: product name \"DealPulse\", subtitle \"MCP Fabric \302\267 Verifiable Handoffs\", demo scenario selector, \"Run Demo\" button\n\nDEMO SCENARIOS (hardcoded fixtures; no real OAuth)\nInclude at least 2 scenarios selectable from dropdown:\nA) \"Expanding enterprise \342\200\224 champion weak\" (medium risk)\nB) \"Late-stage legal block \342\200\224 paper process stalled\" (high risk)\n\nEach scenario includes:\n- Fake CRM opportunity JSON (account, ARR, stage, close date, competitors, stakeholders)\n- A realistic multi-speaker sales call transcript (8\342\200\22315 turns)\n- Expected risk themes already implied in the transcript\n\nAGENT BEHAVIOR\nWhen user clicks \"Run Demo\" or asks \"Analyze this deal\":\n1) Call skill: transcript.analyze\n2) Call skill: crm.get_opportunity\n3) Call skill: meddpicc.extract\n4) Update Risk Panel\n5) Propose 3\342\200\2235 next-best actions\n6) Optionally auto-trigger handoff if risk > 70 OR paper-process/legal gaps exist:\n   - Router \342\206\222 Compliance Specialist agent\n   - Show handoff packet (context summary, decisions so far, open questions, recommended owner)\n7) Offer executable actions as buttons:\n   - crm.update_stage\n   - crm.add_next_steps\n   - email.draft_ae_brief\n   - ticket.create_legal_review (for high paper-process risk)\n8) Every tool call appears in Action Ledger with: timestamp, skill name, inputs summary, outputs summary, status, correlation_id\n\nMCP FABRIC (must be visible and central to the story)\nImplement a Skill Registry with these mock MCP skills (local JS functions, not real network MCP yet):\n- crm.get_opportunity\n- crm.update_stage\n- crm.add_next_steps\n- transcript.analyze\n- meddpicc.extract\n- email.draft_ae_brief\n- ticket.create_legal_review\n- handoff.route_specialist\n- handoff.to_human\n\nEach skill card shows: name, description, input schema (short), output schema (short), \"status: mock MCP\".\n\nHANDOFF OS (capability, not separate product)\nShow a vertical timeline:\n- DealPulse (primary)\n- Compliance Specialist (when routed)\n- Human AE / RevOps (escalation)\nHandoff packet JSON viewer (pretty printed) with fields:\n{\n  from_agent, to_agent, reason, risk_score, meddpicc_gaps, decisions_so_far, open_questions, recommended_actions, evidence_quotes[]\n}\n\nCHAT UX\n- Streaming or stepwise status messages (\"Calling transcript.analyze\342\200\246\", \"Updating risk model\342\200\246\")\n- User can ask follow-ups: \"Why is Economic Buyer weak?\", \"Draft the AE brief\", \"Hand off to compliance\", \"Escalate to human\"\n- Cite 1\342\200\2232 short transcript quotes when explaining gaps\n\nTECH REQUIREMENTS (important for later Cloudflare export)\n- Single deployable frontend app (React or vanilla + modern JS is fine)\n- Keep all fixtures in /fixtures or embedded JSON modules\n- Put mock MCP skills in a clear skills/ or mcp/ module with one function per skill\n- Separate \"agent orchestrator\" logic from UI\n- No secrets required for demo path (optional Gemini API key only if you use live LLM; otherwise rule-based + templated analysis is OK for offline reliability)\n- Prefer deterministic demo mode: \"Run Demo\" should always produce a strong, consistent result for judges even if LLM is unavailable\n- Include a DEMO_MODE flag: if no API key, use fixture-derived analysis templates\n\nDETERMINISTIC ANALYSIS ENGINE (required)\nDo NOT rely only on an LLM. Implement a robust heuristic analyzer that:\n- Scans transcript for keywords/phrases for each MEDDPICC element\n- Computes gap severity\n- Computes risk score\n- Picks next actions from a rules table\nThen optionally enhance wording with LLM if available.\nThis makes the demo reliable for Devpost judges.\n\nSAMPLE OUTPUT QUALITY BAR\nRisk panel must look \"investor/demo ready\":\n- Clear score\n- Specific gaps (\"Champion mentioned but no multi-thread to Economic Buyer\")\n- Evidence quotes\n- Actions with owners and due-style suggestions (\"AE: schedule EB meeting this week\")\n\nREADME SECTION IN UI\nInclude a collapsible \"Architecture\" drawer explaining:\nMCP Fabric (skills) \342\206\222 Orchestrator \342\206\222 DealPulse agent \342\206\222 Handoff router \342\206\222 Action Ledger\nPlus \"Stage 2 roadmap\": Freshworks MCP/Agent Studio, ElevenLabs AE voice brief, real CRM connectors, eval traces.\n\nDELIVERABLES IN CODE\n- App runs locally with npm/vite or equivalent\n- Clear file structure\n- Seed fixtures for both scenarios\n- Comments marking where real MCP/Freshworks would plug in for Stage 2\n\nDo NOT build multiple products. Do NOT add Sarvam/ElevenLabs yet. Do NOT add auth. Focus on one rock-solid happy path.\n\nFirst, scaffold the full app with fixtures + deterministic analyzer + UI panels working end-to-end for scenario B (high risk). Then polish scenario A. Then improve visual polish and microcopy."
    }
  }
