  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Demo Parameters**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the parameters for \"Run Demo\" in scenario B. My primary goal is a cinematic sequence, specifically 20-30 seconds long. I\'m focusing on incorporating status steps for each skill call and dynamically updating the risk panel through animation. These are key considerations in this iteration.\n\n\n**Orchestrating the Sequence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the final actions to create a cohesive sequence. The plan is to trigger an automatic handoff to Compliance and then populate the ledger with at least five entries. After that, a concluding assistant message will present a risk summary, prioritize three actions, and provide call-to-action buttons. It should all function seamlessly in DEMO_MODE without an API key. I\'m focusing on timing and orchestration, ensuring a strong, realistic, and cinematic effect.\n\n\n**Implementing Skill Integration**\n\nI\'m currently working on integrating the `ticket.create_legal_review` and `crm.update_stage` calls into the sequence. I\'m focusing on the visual feedback, specifically the active skill chip in the MCP Registry and ensuring intermediate chat log messages or streaming steps clearly show the agent\'s thought process, including verbatim quotes and parameter displays.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Animation & Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating animations and ledger data into the flow. Specifically, I\'m working on animating deal gaps into the risk panel, each with a critical redline badge. Simultaneously, I\'m defining the automatic handoff to Compliance, which updates the timeline, generates a handoff packet with checksum, open legal questions, decisions, and transcript citations. Lastly, I am adding at least five ledger entries to be displayed in the panel in real time.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Action Items**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the concluding assistant message. I\'ve defined the risk breakdown, noting the critical blocker and root causes. My focus is on clearly outlining the top three recommended actions, directly linking them to the skills they trigger, like the `ticket.create_legal_review` call to route the EU data residency addendum. I\'m prioritizing clarity and direct action.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 977315544
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
