    thinking: "**Constructing the Orchestrator**\n\nI\'m currently focused on constructing the cinematic orchestrator within `src/engine/orchestrator.ts`. I\'ve made sure the `sleep` helper function integrates smoothly with async/await, using the provided example. Now, I\'m defining the precise step-by-step sequence for Scenario B, working out the details.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Audio**\n\nI\'ve initiated the audio analysis phase. At t=0, a notification message kicks off the orchestration, detailing the target opportunity and key participants. The system begins by parsing the 12 speaker turns and acoustic sentiment, logging this action to the ledger. Currently, the initial score is 20 with low severity, analyzing partial items, with the first step complete.\n\n\n**Evaluating Liability Cap**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details of Section 7.2 regarding the liability cap, considering the implications of the Thursday 5 PM cutoff. At t=4s, I\'m syncing the CRM pipeline, history, and competitor data to refine the initial state. The score is at 45 (medium severity), and metrics have been validated. This is logged to the action ledger as the second entry.\n\n\n**Assessing the Critical Risk**\n\nI\'ve determined critical MEDDPICC gaps exist. Specifically, Rachel Thorne rejected the Standard DPA, leading to a 5x liability cap request due to BaFin telemetry. The deadline for the addendum is Thursday at 5 PM CET, or the deal slips to Q4. My risk score is now 84/100. At t=13s, the CRM stage was updated and the risk flagged, and at t=17s, routing to a compliance specialist began.\n\n\n**Routing the Specialists**\n\nI\'ve completed routing to the Compliance Specialist Agent, logging this step (Ledger Entry #5) with the updated Handoffs timeline. A handoff packet, `#PKG-8821-B`, has been generated with its checksum. Now, I\'m at t=22s, and invoking `ticket.create_legal_review` and `crm.add_next_steps`. These generate legal artifacts (Ledger Entries #6 and #7), including legal ticket `#LEG-9941` for review with an SLA. CRM is being updated.\n\n\n"
