  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial scope for the README file. I\'ve pinpointed the core value proposition: DealPulse, an enterprise deal-risk agent built on a reusable MCP fabric. The guiding principle is \"Build skills once. Any agent can\". This sets the stage for a clear and concise overview section.\n\n\n**Outlining the Architecture**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the architectural components. There\'s a client presentation layer (React 19, Tailwind, etc.), a decoupled MCP Skills Registry, the DealPulse Orchestration Engine, an Action Ledger for audit trails, and a Handoffs OS for incident transfer. Now, I\'m focusing on the component breakdown, modularity, and formal input/output schemas for each of the tools.\n\n\n**Detailing the Deployment**\n\nI\'m now detailing deployment steps. I\'ve documented local development (using `npm install`, `npm run dev`) and Cloudflare Pages deployment with build commands and environment variables. I\342\200\231ve included detailed instructions for both Cloudflare Dashboard and Wrangler CLI deployment.\n\n**Mapping out the Roadmap**\n\nI\'m currently outlining the stage-2 roadmap. Key areas include distributed persistence (Cloudflare D1/KV/Firestore), real-time audio ingestion with Gemini Live API, bi-directional MCP integration with CRMs and collaboration tools, and automated escalation workflows. I\'m focusing on these for the future of DealPulse.\n\n**Creating the Demonstration**\n\nMy current focus is crafting the demo script. It will showcase a quick walkthrough, using a specific scenario (GlobalFin Technologies \342\200\224 $350k legal block). The user will be able to click \"Run Demo\" to see real-time skill orchestration.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 586905989
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
